    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter tonight\u2019s slate with **Christian Yelich** leading the charge as our most confident start. Carrying a 75.84 efficiency score, **Yelich** benefits from a high-ceiling matchup against Feltner, where a generous SP skill projection (+19%) and a significant platoon edge (+13%) align to provide our best opportunity for production. **Junior Caminero** (69.49) and **Colt Keith** (68.51) follow closely behind; **Caminero** continues to command the lineup due to an elite .376 xwOBA that helps him mitigate a slight park disadvantage, while **Colt Keith** leverages a prime leadoff spot and a soft matchup against Wacha to anchor the top of our order. \n\nConversely, we are proceeding with caution regarding **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (58.30) and **Trea Turner** (58.46). While both possess the speed necessary to address our league-wide scarcity in stolen bases, they face legitimate ace-level threats in Skenes and Weathers, respectively. The heavy SP skill penalties (-19% and -13%) underscore the risk, though **Crow-Armstrong** remains a lock for his defensive speed utility. **Casey Schmitt** (63.92) is our situational X-factor today, as a favorable wind forecast at his venue boosts his profile, vaulting him ahead of alternatives despite his lower base projection.\n\nThe most difficult roster decision involved **Josh Smith**, who sits on the bench with a 45.38 score. While **Smith** provides a strong platoon advantage (+14%) against the right-handed Woo, his historical efficiency metrics couldn't quite eclipse the cumulative value of **Carson Benge** or **Chase Meidroth** in today's specific configuration. Elsewhere, we continue to monitor the status of **Hyeseong Kim**, who remains unavailable in the Oklahoma City system. With high-intensity matchups against arms like Skenes, we are managing our game caps carefully, ensuring that high-floor performers like **Yordan Alvarez** (63.49) remain slotted in to provide the consistent power output needed to maintain our Roto standing.",
